\section{Result fields}{

\code{items} contains \code{set_id}, \code{item_id}, \code{global_item_id}, \code{theta_link_mean},
\code{theta_link_sd}, \code{theta_link_lower}, \code{theta_link_upper}, and \code{rank_link}.
\code{theta_link_eap} is a compatibility alias of \code{theta_link_mean}; it is a
posterior mean for E1 and E3-MCMC, and a MAP location for E2/E3 Laplace.
\code{estimator_id} and \code{uncertainty_scope} accompany every item.
\code{offset} contains \code{delta_mean}, \code{delta_sd}, \code{delta_lower}, \code{delta_upper}, and
\code{identification} (\code{prior_only}, \code{cross_set}, \code{unidentified}, or \code{failed}).
At zero cross edges a valid result retains the configured Normal offset prior
and reports \code{prior_only}. E1 retains fixed shapes; E2 retains independent full
Gaussian Phase A bridges; E3 fits only the centered Phase A shape posterior.

\code{uncertainty} contains the named free-coordinate \code{covariance} (or \code{NULL}),
\code{basis}, and \code{item_transform}. For transform T and covariance V, item-scale
covariance is \code{T \%*\% V \%*\% t(T)}. E1's item transform has only a delta column;
its fixed shapes supply the deterministic part of item means.

\code{diagnostics} records \code{fit_attempted}, \code{fit_valid}, \code{convergence_code},
\code{finite_objective}, \code{finite_gradient}, \code{hessian_pd}, \code{covariance_valid},
\code{covariance_jitter}, \code{warning_code}, \code{failure_code}, \code{uncertainty_scope},
\code{sampler}, \code{elapsed_seconds}, \code{cpu_seconds}, \code{peak_memory_bytes}, and
\code{n_parameters}. Undefined fields use typed missing values. Invalid fits carry
a failure code and cannot be used for prediction. E1 adds optional
\code{quadrature} diagnostics: method, domain, coordinate, effective controls,
integration partitions, subdivision count, log normalizer, estimated mass/
moment errors, CDF error and root brackets when computed, summary method,
and status. Partial diagnostics remain available after numerical failure.
Quadrature errors are numerical estimates, not posterior SDs. Valid E1 scope is
\code{offset_only_conditional_on_fixed_shapes}; valid E2/E3 scope is
\code{joint_shapes_and_offset}. A true zero conditional variance is allowed.
E2 adds \code{bridge} diagnostics for each set (draw count, reduced mean,
stabilized covariance, variance scale, and applied jitter) and \code{optimization}
diagnostics (effective controls, starts, convergence, objectives, gradients,
observed Hessians, selected attempt, and reciprocal condition estimates).
Gradients and Hessians are in bridge-whitened coordinates; result covariance
